## Best Practices

### 1. Always Use Proper Escaping
- Never generate Maven commands without proper PowerShell escaping
- Always test commands in PowerShell before providing them to users
- Use backticks for escaping quotes within quoted strings

### 2. Command Structure
- Place system properties after the main Maven command
- Group related properties together
- Use consistent formatting for readability

### 3. Error Handling
- Include `-DfailIfNoTests=false` when running specific test patterns
- Use `-Dmaven.test.failure.ignore=true` to continue on test failures
- Consider using `-Dmaven.test.skip=true` for build-only operations

### 4. Performance Optimization
- Use `-T 1C` for parallel builds (one thread per CPU core)
- Use `-o` for offline mode when dependencies are already downloaded
- Use `-q` for quiet mode in CI/CD pipelines

